<title>BAHRAIN: Saudi American Bank Q1 net profit rises.</title>
<headline>Saudi American Bank Q1 net profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-04-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			   (million Saudi riyals)</p>
<p> Net profit		  265.2   vs    243.2</p>
<p> Operating income	  754.4   vs    795.6</p>
<p> Expenses		    548.9   vs    568.2</p>
<p> Net operating income    205.5   vs    227.4</p>
<p> Other income		 59.7   vs     15.8</p>
<p> Shareholders' funds   4,581.7   vs  4,320.0</p>
<p> Assets		   41,533.8   vs 41,854.8</p>
<p>Full Name: Saudi American Bank.</p>
<p>Note - The Riyadh-based bank, the biggest joint venture bank in Saudi Arabia, is 30 percent owned by Citibank, part of U.S. banking giant Citicorp.</p>
</text>
